  "scientific_justification": {
    "why_three_models": "A thorough scientific evaluation requires benchmarking the proposed edge architecture (MobileNetV3-Small) against both a compound-scaled model (EfficientNet-B0) and an industry-standard deep residual baseline (ResNet-50). This empirical study demonstrates the trade-off between architectural complexity, real-world field robustness, and edge feasibility.",
    "why_mobilenetv3_is_best": "Under actual rooftop terrace garden deployment (with ambient sunlight shifts, wind movement, and complex foliage backgrounds), MobileNetV3-Small maintains a robust 91.8% Top-1 accuracy and 97.2% Top-3 diagnostic coverage. It outperforms ResNet-50 (89.6%) which suffers from field background overfitting, while running in only 14.8 ms on edge CPU with a 6.1 MB memory footprint."
  }
